[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Italian Game: Two Knights Defense"]
[ECO "C57"]
[Character "sharp,tactical"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "trap,fork"]
[Themes "centre-counter,give-back-material"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 3... Nf6 { A second option, and a sharp one. Our course plays 3...Bc5 instead, so this line is only shown and never drilled. } 4. Ng5 { Threatens Nxf7. } 4... d5 { Strikes in the centre and blocks the bishop's diagonal to f7. }
5. exd5 5... Na5 { Chases the bishop away. Never play 5...Nxd5? 6.Nxf7, the Fried Liver Attack, which wins for White. }
( 5... Nxd5? 6. Nxf7 Kxf7 7. Qf3+ Ke6 8. Nc3 )
6. Bb5+ 6... c6 { Hits the bishop and the pawn on d5 together. } 7. dxc6 7... bxc6 8. Be2 8... h6 { Asks the knight on g5 to leave before it can go to f7. } 9. Nf3 9... e4 { Hits the knight again and opens the bishop on c8. } 10. Ne5 10... Bd6 { Attacks the knight again and prepares to castle. Black is a pawn down but has the better development. } *
